<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tughril III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1194</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril</a> III was the last Seljuk sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, reigning from 1176 to 1194. For most of his reign real power lay with the Eldiguzid atabegs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, who had placed him on the throne. His attempts to rule in his own right led to imprisonment and further conflict, and in 1194 he was defeated and killed near Ray by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a> Tekish, ending Seljuk rule in Iran.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tughril-iii.jpg" alt="Tughril III" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Author: Benjamin Banayan (rugrabbit.com), photographed at the Metropolitan Museum of Art exhibit &quot;COURT AND COSMOS: T... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tughril_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
